Maintainer: MCC45TR <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), g++, make, pkg-config, libsystemd-dev (>= 257), libssl-dev, libdrm-dev
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/MCC45TR/uke-linux-hardware-support

Package: uke-battery-observer
Architecture: arm64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, systemd, dbus
Description: Uke read-only battery telemetry
 Native device helper. Software packaging does not establish physical
 qualification. Firmware calibration and charging controls are not included.

Package: uke-charge-control
Architecture: arm64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, systemd, udev, upower (>= 1.91.5), uke-upower-battery-abi-1, uke-kernel-charge-admission-abi-1
Description: evidence-gated native Uke charge control
 Retains the shared unqualified profile and exact per-boot identity gates.
 Threshold and current services remain disabled by default. Voltage and PD
 remain firmware-owned. No calibration or physical acceptance is supplied.

Package: uke-offline-charge
Architecture: arm64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, systemd, uke-boot-offline-charge-abi-1
Description: native Uke offline charger screen
 Retains the isolated charger target and exact boot-mode marker. The normal
 boot target is never changed by package installation. A matched initramfs
 must separately admit charger boot; device qualification remains pending.
